{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 1569 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "34a9cd22b5bfbe7a9d338848708adac49e84e248163cf3e6743ec67ff2ec8838" :edb/db-before-t 1568 :edb/db-after-t 1569 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534881 50 #inst "2026-10-08T09:57:59.278Z" 13194139534881 true] [17592186175876 1020 #edb/ref 17592186317082 13194139534881 true] [17592186175876 1020 #edb/ref 17592186317089 13194139534881 true] [17592186175877 1020 #edb/ref 17592186317092 13194139534881 true] [17592186176479 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534881 true] [17592186176479 1100 "> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question.\n\nA particle $P$ moves along the $x$-axis and its velocity at time $t > 0$ is given by $v(t) = 4t + 3t^{2}$. At time $t = 1$ the particle is located at the position $x = 12$. What is the position of the particle at time $t = 4$?" 13194139534881 false] [17592186176479 1100 "A particle $P$ moves along the $x$-axis and its velocity at time $t>0$ is given by $v(t)=4t+3{t}^{2}.$ At time $t=1$ the particle is located at the position $x=12.$ What is the position of the particle at time $t=4?$" 13194139534881 true] [17592186176479 1145 "The position of the particle at $t=4$ is equal to its position at $t=1$ plus the total displacement over $t\\in [1,4].$ Therefore, we can calculate it as follows:\n\n$$\nx(4)=x(1)+{\\int }_{1}^{4}v(t)\\,\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nCarrying out the computations, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(4) & =12+{\\int }_{1}^{4}(4t+3{t}^{2})\\text{d}t \\\\  & =12+[2{t}^{2}+{t}^{3}]_{1}^{4} \\\\  & =12+([2(4)^{2}+{4}^{3}]-[2(1)^{2}+{1}^{3}]) \\\\  & =12+([32+64]-[2+1]) \\\\  & =12+(96-3) \\\\  & =12+93 \\\\  & =105\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the position of the particle at $t=4$ is $x=105.$" 13194139534881 true] [17592186176497 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534881 true] [17592186176497 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042727/assets/6c0f74fa4820cd8e6945666ab90e0eafac4cc1ada7578fb5a053f197adf08084.png)\n\nThe graph above shows the velocity of an object moving in a straight line along the $x$-axis. At time $t=1$ the particle is located at the position $x=2.$ What is the position of the particle at time $t=7?$" 13194139534881 true] [17592186176497 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/3576/Source/Images/q-81515.png)\n\nThe graph above shows the velocity of an object moving in a straight line along the $x$-axis. At time $t = 1$ the particle is located at the position $x = 2$. What is the position of the particle at time $t = 7$?" 13194139534881 false] [17592186176497 1145 "The position of the particle at $t=7$ is equal to its position at $t=1$ plus the total displacement over $t\\in [1,7].$ Therefore, we can calculate it as follows:\n\n$$\nx(7)=x(1)+{\\int }_{1}^{7}v(t)\\,\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nWe are told that $x(1)=2$, and we can compute the integral ${\\int }_{1}^{7}v(t)\\,\\text{d}t$ by finding the signed area under the graph from $t=1$ to $t=7.$ Computing the signed area, we get\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{1}^{7}v(t)\\,\\text{d}t=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nx(7)=2+0=2\n$$\n\nSo the position of the particle at $t=7$ is $x=2.$" 13194139534881 true] [17592186317082 1017 #edb/ref 17592186317083 13194139534881 true] [17592186317082 1089 "q-2414" 13194139534881 true] [17592186317082 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534881 true] [17592186317082 1100 "A particle $P$ moves along the $x$-axis and its velocity at time $t>0$ is given by $v(t)=3{t}^{2}-6t.$ \nAt time $t=2,$ the particle is located at the position $x=6.$ What is the position of the particle at time $t=5?$" 13194139534881 true] [17592186317082 1113 #uuid "f6eb5e12-95ae-5b0b-b902-abc4f32a452e" 13194139534881 true] [17592186317082 1145 "The position of the particle at $t=5$ is equal to its position at $t=2$ plus the total displacement over $t\\in [2,5].$ Therefore, we can calculate it as follows:\n\n$$\nx(5)=x(2)+{\\int }_{2}^{5}v(t)\\,\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nCarrying out the computations, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(5) & =6+{\\int }_{2}^{5}(3{t}^{2}-6t)\\,\\text{dt} \\\\  & =6+{[{t}^{3}-3{t}^{2}]}_{2}^{5} \\\\  & =6+([(5)^{3}-3(5)^{2}]-[(2)^{3}-3(2)^{2}]) \\\\  & =6+([125-75]-[8-12]) \\\\  & =6+(50-(-4)) \\\\  & =6+54 \\\\  & =60.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the position of the particle at $t=5$ is $x=60.$" 13194139534881 true] [17592186317083 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317084 13194139534881 true] [17592186317083 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317085 13194139534881 true] [17592186317083 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317086 13194139534881 true] [17592186317083 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317087 13194139534881 true] [17592186317083 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317088 13194139534881 true] [17592186317083 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534881 true] [17592186317083 1041 "selection" 13194139534881 true] [17592186317083 1104 #edb/ref 17592186317084 13194139534881 true] [17592186317083 1110 #uuid "e219cc7c-efca-5b68-a953-c7be185a35fd" 13194139534881 true] [17592186317084 1034 "60" 13194139534881 true] [17592186317084 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534881 true] [17592186317084 1111 #uuid "fabd2315-8992-5aff-9fa8-2e74d74dc8c0" 13194139534881 true] [17592186317085 1034 "79" 13194139534881 true] [17592186317085 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534881 true] [17592186317085 1111 #uuid "32477030-d71f-5818-97a9-8b0aa169f002" 13194139534881 true] [17592186317086 1034 "52" 13194139534881 true] [17592186317086 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534881 true] [17592186317086 1111 #uuid "594f1c75-af20-5181-adf4-34c8e56fdfcd" 13194139534881 true] [17592186317087 1034 "56" 13194139534881 true] [17592186317087 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534881 true] [17592186317087 1111 #uuid "47c09873-8d1d-5704-9552-70a5ff56f885" 13194139534881 true] [17592186317088 1034 "68" 13194139534881 true] [17592186317088 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534881 true] [17592186317088 1111 #uuid "85101206-7aba-5c7c-a07a-5982a3bac415" 13194139534881 true] [17592186317089 1017 #edb/ref 17592186317090 13194139534881 true] [17592186317089 1089 "q-351449" 13194139534881 true] [17592186317089 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534881 true] [17592186317089 1100 "A particle $Q$ moves along the $x$-axis and its velocity at time $t\\ge 0$ is given by $v(t)=6t-{t}^{2}.$ At time $t=3$ the particle is located at the position $x=2.$ \nFind the position of the particle at time $t=6.$\n\nThe position of the particle at $t=6$ is $x=$\n{{field-1}}." 13194139534881 true] [17592186317089 1113 #uuid "a73379bf-3cdc-5ce7-a08f-2ee49976d4da" 13194139534881 true] [17592186317089 1145 "The position of the particle at $t=6$ is equal to its position at $t=3$ plus the total displacement over $t\\in [3,6].$ Therefore, we can calculate it as follows:\n\n$$\nx(6)=x(3)+{\\int }_{3}^{6}v(t)\\,\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nCarrying out the computations, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(6) & =2+{\\int }_{3}^{6}(6t-{t}^{2})\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =2+{[3{t}^{2}-\\frac{1}{3}{t}^{3}]}_{3}^{6} \\\\  & =2+[3(6)^{2}-\\frac{1}{3}(6)^{3}]-[3(3)^{2}-\\frac{1}{3}(3)^{3}] \\\\  & =2+36-18 \\\\  & =2+18 \\\\  & =20.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the position of the particle at $t=6$ is $x=20.$" 13194139534881 true] [17592186317090 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317091 13194139534881 true] [17592186317090 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534881 true] [17592186317090 1041 "field-1" 13194139534881 true] [17592186317090 1104 #edb/ref 17592186317091 13194139534881 true] [17592186317090 1110 #uuid "3eb12efc-13bb-58f0-a351-872e3384d0f9" 13194139534881 true] [17592186317091 1034 "20" 13194139534881 true] [17592186317091 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534881 true] [17592186317091 1111 #uuid "2567e6eb-702c-57e9-8a35-65faf7c4a5b0" 13194139534881 true] [17592186317092 1017 #edb/ref 17592186317093 13194139534881 true] [17592186317092 1089 "q-81510" 13194139534881 true] [17592186317092 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534881 true] [17592186317092 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042727/assets/e484bfde797b94d298227bac9ae25fb68a3de5698e7f8d8527e37e11cb051a95.png)\n\nThe graph above shows the velocity of an object moving in a straight line along the $x$-axis. At time $t=2$ the particle is located at the position $x=1.$ What is the position of the particle at time $t=8?$" 13194139534881 true] [17592186317092 1113 #uuid "ffb15d24-7ff5-58bf-b04b-310e248ca644" 13194139534881 true] [17592186317092 1145 "The position of the particle at $t=8$ is equal to its position at $t=2$ plus the total displacement over $t\\in [2,8].$ Therefore, we can calculate it as follows:\n\n$$\nx(8)=x(2)+{\\int }_{2}^{8}v(t)\\,\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nWe are told that $x(2)=1$, and we can compute the integral ${\\int }_{2}^{8}v(t)\\,\\text{d}t$ by finding the signed area under the graph from $t=2$ to $t=8.$ Computing the signed area, we get\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{2}^{8}v(t)\\,\\text{d}t=14.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nx(8)=1+14=15\n$$\n\nSo the position of the particle at $t=8$ is $x=15.$" 13194139534881 true] [17592186317093 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317094 13194139534881 true] [17592186317093 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317095 13194139534881 true] [17592186317093 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317096 13194139534881 true] [17592186317093 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317097 13194139534881 true] [17592186317093 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317098 13194139534881 true] [17592186317093 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534881 true] [17592186317093 1041 "selection" 13194139534881 true] [17592186317093 1104 #edb/ref 17592186317096 13194139534881 true] [17592186317093 1110 #uuid "9055f599-2064-5028-bdc6-515c45c30cd5" 13194139534881 true] [17592186317094 1034 "12" 13194139534881 true] [17592186317094 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534881 true] [17592186317094 1111 #uuid "4dc13e5a-fe0a-5c09-92ac-0461142173ef" 13194139534881 true] [17592186317095 1034 "16" 13194139534881 true] [17592186317095 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534881 true] [17592186317095 1111 #uuid "61de2e41-98c9-5655-ba4f-d250c67d67ba" 13194139534881 true] [17592186317096 1034 "15" 131941